              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20–25</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Cool-down</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Back to warm-up speed, then slowest</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1–2</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h3>Session B: Gentle incline walk (25 minutes)</h3>
          <p>
            A small grade makes each step more work without speeding you up, which many older
            walkers find steadier than walking faster. Keep the grade low: 1 to 3% is plenty in
            this plan. If you have knee or hip arthritis, or a recent joint replacement, check with
            your physical therapist before adding incline at all.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Minutes</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What to do</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Speed</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Incline</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Effort</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0–5</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Warm-up</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lowest comfortable, rising slowly</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1–3</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">5–9</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Flat walk</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Comfortable pace</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">9–13</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Gentle hill</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Same, or 0.1–0.2 mph slower</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1–2%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">5</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">13–17</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Slightly steeper</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Same as above</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">2–3%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">5–6</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">17–20</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Back down</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Comfortable pace</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4–5</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20–25</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Cool-down</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Warm-up speed, then slowest</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1–2</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h3>Session C: Short intervals (24 minutes)</h3>
          <p>
            Short spells of brisker walking with easy walking in between. These are not sprints:
            the "brisk" minutes are only 0.2 to 0.5 mph above your comfortable pace, and you should
            still be able to speak in short phrases throughout. Change speed in 0.1 mph steps and
            keep one hand near the rail while the belt adjusts.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
